.TH fsck.briefs 8

.SH NAME
.PP
fsck.briefs - Check and repair a BrieFS filesystem


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
fsck.briefs

.PP
.RS

.nf
[--assume-yes|-y]
[--help|-h]
[--no|-n]
[--optimize]
[--preen|-p]
[--repair-only]=[value]
[--repair|-r]
[--type|-t]=[value]
[--verbose|-V]
[--version|-v]

.fi
.RE


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Check and, with --repair, fix a BrieFS filesystem on DEVICE.  fsck.briefs verifies journal-record and B+ tree checksums, validates directory-trie pages, inode extended-attribute chains, and inode link counts, and can rebuild the allocator bitmaps and B+ tree extent indexes, compact directory tries, and repair link counts.  Repairs are phased and selectable with --repair-only.

.PP
\fBUsage\fP:

.PP
.RS

.nf
fsck.briefs [global options] DEVICE

.fi
.RE


.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--assume-yes, -y\fP: do not ask for confirmation before modifying the volume

.PP
\fB--help, -h\fP: show help

.PP
\fB--no, -n\fP: read-only check; do not attempt repairs (default mode, made explicit for fsck(8) -n)

.PP
\fB--optimize\fP: safe compaction only (alias for --repair --repair-only=trie,extents)

.PP
\fB--preen, -p\fP: non-interactive repair; alias for --repair --assume-yes

.PP
\fB--repair, -r\fP: attempt to repair found errors

.PP
\fB--repair-only\fP="": run only selected repair phases (comma-separated: allocator,btrees,btree-rebuild,btree-orphan,extents,trie,links; default all)

.PP
\fB--type, -t\fP="": filesystem type (accepted for fsck(8) compatibility; ignored)

.PP
\fB--verbose, -V\fP: verbose output

.PP
\fB--version, -v\fP: print the version
